Implemented the full rebuild orchestration/reporting shell and UI visibility, but did not make real device calls. The repo safety rules explicitly block automated Codex tasks from contacting or modifying real infrastructure, so the generated reports show that blocker instead of using mock substitutes.

Changed:
- Added `make provider-lab-full-rebuild`
- Added `app/backend/scripts/full_device_rebuild_workflow.py`
- Added `app/backend/app/services/full_rebuild_run.py`
- Added `GET /api/v1/lab/full-rebuild-summary`
- Updated Provider Status UI with a “Full Lab Rebuild Run” panel
- Updated `app/docs/workflows.md`

Generated reports:
- `artifacts/codex-runs/full-device-rebuild-baseline-report.md`
- `artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-full-bootstrap-report.md`
- `artifacts/codex-runs/hpe-full-rebuild-ilo-report.md`
- `artifacts/codex-runs/hpe-full-rebuild-raid-report.md`
- `artifacts/codex-runs/esxi-full-rebuild-boot-report.md`
- `artifacts/codex-runs/full-device-rebuild-4h-report.md`
- `artifacts/codex-runs/full-device-rebuild-4h-summary-redacted.json`

Validation:
- `make provider-lab-full-rebuild` passed and wrote the reports
- `make backend-test` passed: 193 tests
- `npm run build` passed
- Screenshot captured: `artifacts/screenshots/full-rebuild-provider-status-loaded.png`

Current final status: blocked by safety policy, not by mock substitution. The Cisco historical report still shows the concrete live blocker: exec prompt reached, but privileged exec was not confirmed. Goal usage: 222,695 tokens, about 5 minutes elapsed.
